        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:IAO_0000589</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">An alternative name for a class or property which is unique across the OBO Foundry.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:IAO_0000589</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal xml:lang="en">The intended usage of that property is as follow: OBO foundry unique labels are automatically generated based on regular expressions provided by each ontology, so that SO could specify unique label = &apos;sequence &apos; + [label], etc. , MA could specify &apos;mouse + [label]&apos; etc. Upon importing terms, ontology developers can choose to use the &apos;OBO foundry unique label&apos; for an imported term or not. The same applies to tools .</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
