        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0000916</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The subdivision of the vertebrate body between the thorax and pelvis. The ventral part of the abdomen contains the abdominal cavity and visceral organs. The dorsal part includes the abdominal section of the vertebral column.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0000916</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Vertebrate specific. In arthropods &apos;abdomen&apos; is the most distal section of the body which lies behind the thorax or cephalothorax. If need be we can introduce some grouping class</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
