        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0001128</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A paired muscle in the superficial layers of the anterior portion of the neck. It acts to flex and rotate the head. It also acts as an accessory muscle of inspiration, along with the scalene muscles of the neck. [WP,unvetted].</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000116"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0001128</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>TODO: sternocleidomastoid = sternomastoid + Cleidomastoideus. Origin: from manubrium sterni (sterno) and clavicle (cleido) and it&apos;s insertion at the mastoid process of the temporal bone.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000412"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0001128</AbbreviatedIRI>
