    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:UBPROP_0000001"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003699</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Medial attachment of the two halves of the pelvic girdle.[AAO]</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:UBPROP_0000008"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003699</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>In birds, the pubic symphysis is present only in the ostrich, and the two hip bones are usually widely separated, making it easier to lay large eggs - Romer, Alfred Sherwood; Parsons, Thomas S. (1977). The Vertebrate Body. Philadelphia, PA: Holt-Saunders International. pp. 188-192. ISBN 0-03-910284-X.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
