    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003729</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>A mucous membrane that lines the mouth.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000232"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003729</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>this is defined as any mucous membrane of the mouth - including palate, lips, uvula, etc. ncit split mouth/oral mucosa into lip and buccal. In future we may split into masticatory/keratinized (gingiva + hard palate) vs lining/non-keratinized (lips, cheeks, floor of mouth, soft palate). FMA distinguishes between mucosa of mouth and region of mouth (the latter including the buccal mucosa)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000412"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003729</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:uberon.owl</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:RO_0002175"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003729</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:NCBITaxon_9606</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:UBPROP_0000001"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0003729</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>the mucous membrane epithelium of the mouth. It can be divided into three categories: masticatory, lining, and specialized[Wikipedia:Oral_mucosa].</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
