        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795285</IRI>
        <Literal>A vertical line running along the midline of the anterior body surface, aligned with the sternum. On the anterior abdominal and chest walls, the anterior median line can be seen extending from the jugular notch, crossing over the sternum and linea alba in their midline, and reaching out to the midline pubic symphysis.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
