    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795319</IRI>
        <Literal>The scapular region refers to the area on the posterior thoracic wall corresponding to the location of the scapula (shoulder blade). It encompasses the structures overlying and surrounding the scapula, including associated muscles such as the trapezius, deltoid, and rotator cuff muscles.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795319</IRI>
        <Literal>scapular region</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795320</IRI>
        <Literal>The supratragic tubercle is a small prominence on the auricle of the ear, located just above the tragus. It serves as an anatomical landmark and can vary in size and shape between individuals.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795320</IRI>
        <Literal>supratragic tubercle</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795321</IRI>
        <Literal>The anatomical space between the seventh and eighth ribs, containing intercostal muscles, vessels, and nerves.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
