        <Literal>iliotibial band</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795325</IRI>
        <Literal>The tibialis anterior tendon is the tendon of the tibialis anterior muscle, located on the front of the lower leg. It passes along the ankle and inserts on the medial cuneiform and the first metatarsal. This tendon enables dorsiflexion and inversion of the foot. The tibialis anterior tendon (TAT) begins at the distal one-third of the tibia. It is the most medial tendon of the ankle and foot.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0112785"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795325</IRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0000978</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
