        <Literal>Fossa jugularis</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="NIFRID:synonym"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795331</IRI>
        <Literal>Interclavicular fossa</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="NIFRID:synonym"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795331</IRI>
        <Literal>Jugular notch</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795331</IRI>
        <Literal>suprasternal fossa</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795332</IRI>
        <Literal>The anterior skin fold of the elbow, marking the transition between the upper arm and forearm, overlying the cubital fossa.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795332</IRI>
        <Literal>cubital crease</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795333</IRI>
        <Literal>The dorsal wrist crease is the skin fold that forms on the back (dorsal) side of the wrist, often visible when the hand is extended. It marks the junction between the forearm and the hand and is located near the proximal ends of the metacarpal bones.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795333</IRI>
        <Literal>dorsal wrist crease</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795334</IRI>
        <Literal>The palmar wrist crease is the transverse skin fold that appears on the palm side of the wrist when the hand is flexed. It marks the boundary between the forearm and the palm and is located approximately at the level of the distal radius and ulna.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795334</IRI>
        <Literal>palmar wrist crease</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795335</IRI>
        <Literal>The tendon of the muscle that abducts and extends the thumb, located in the posterior compartment of the forearm.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795335</IRI>
        <Literal>abductor pollicis longus tendon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795336</IRI>
        <Literal>The tendon of the muscle extending the proximal phalanx of the thumb, positioned laterally in the forearm.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795336</IRI>
        <Literal>extensor pollicis brevis tendon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty IRI="http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0112785"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795337</IRI>
        <Literal>The tendon of the muscle responsible for extending the thumb at the interphalangeal joint.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795337</IRI>
        <Literal>extensor pollicis longus tendon</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="obo:IAO_0000115"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795338</IRI>
        <Literal>The lateral supracondylar ridge (lateral supraepicondylar ridge or lateral supracondylar crest) is the sharp, prominent margin located along the lateral aspect of the distal end of the body of the humerus. It is the less curved of the two supracondylar ridges of the humerus, the other being the medial supracondylar ridge.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="ilxr:type"/>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795338</IRI>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/readable/type/term</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
