        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0000033</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>B 4</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Bladder 4</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>UB 4</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Urinary Bladder 4</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasVasculatureDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The frontal artery and vein.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0598260</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>BL 4</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dcterms:bibliographicCitation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 122. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>膈關(关,関)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Dysphagia, hiccup, vomiting, belching, pain and stiffness of the back.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the sixth and seventh thoracic nerves; deeper, their lateral branches.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the seventh thoracic vertebra (T7), 3 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line. Note: BL 46, BL17 and GV9 are located at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the seventh thoracic vertebra (T7).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7525476</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture obliquely 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0607588</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Geguan</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
