        <Literal>Front-Mu Point of the Kidney Role</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dc:description"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>An acupuncture point that is located along the Gallbladder Meridian of Foot-Shaoyang (GB), which consists of 44 standardized acupoints beginning at GB 1 (Tongziliao) on the head in the depression lateral to the outer canthus of the eye, zigzagging across the temporal and occipital regions of the head and descending along the lateral side of the neck, trunk, and leg, and ending at GB 44 (Zuqiaoyin) on the lateral side of the fourth toe near the corner of the nail.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dcterms:bibliographicCitation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5283975</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Acupoint of the gallbladder meridian of foot-shaoyang</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Acupuncture point of the gallbladder meridian</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Acupuncture point of the gallbladder meridian of foot-shaoyang</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>GB</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1926756</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Acupoint of the Gallbladder Meridian</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dcterms:bibliographicCitation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1985889</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 105. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1985889</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>大杼</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1985889</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9719785</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1985889</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Headache, pain in the neck and back, pain and soreness in the scapular region, cough, fever, neck rigidity.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1985889</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The medial cutaneous branches of the posterior rami of the first and second thoracic nerves; deeper, their lateral cutaneous branches.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_1985889</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>In the upper back region, at the same level as the inferior border of the spinous process of the first thoracic vertebra (T1), 1.5 B-cun lateral to the posterior median line.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
