        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 51. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>氣(气,気)舍(舎)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Sore throat, pain and rigidity of the neck, asthma, hiccup, goiter.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The medial supraclavicular nerve and the muscular branch of ansa cervicalis.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>In the anterior region of the neck, in the lesser supraclavicular fossa, superior to the sternal end of the clavicle, in the depression between the sternal and clavicular heads of the sternocleidomastoid muscle. Note 1: The sternocleidomastoid muscle is more distinct when the head is turned to the opposite side against resistance. Note 2: ST11 is located superior to the clavicle, inferior to St9.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6221269</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture perpendicularly 0.3-0.5 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Qishe</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasRelatedLocation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4369524</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0000974</AbbreviatedIRI>
