        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 172. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>瞳子髎(髎)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Headache, redness and pain of the eyes, failing of vision, lacrimation, deviation of the eye and mouth.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The zygomaticofacial and zygomaticotemporal nerve, the temporal branch of the facial nerve.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>On the head, in the depression, 0.5 B-cun lateral to the outer canthus of the eye.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5283975</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture subcutaneously 0.3-0.5 inch.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_5541141</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Tongziliao</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
