        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6846652</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>BL 49</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dcterms:bibliographicCitation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 73. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>地機(机)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4598552</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Abdominal pain and distension, diarrhea, edema, dysuria, nocturnal emission, irregular menstruation, dysmenorrhea.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>See Sanyinjiao (SP 6).</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>On the tibial aspect of the leg, posterior to the medial border of the tibia, 3 B-cun inferior to SP9. Note: SP8 is located at the junction of the upper one third and lower two thirds of the line connecting the apex of the patella with the prominence of the medial malleolus.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4167850</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Diji</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasRelatedLocation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0000979</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasRelatedLocation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6848518</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>obo:UBERON_0002446</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
