        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 71. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 7, Acupuncture Points of the Taiyin and Yangming Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>公孫(孙)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6993030</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9493899</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Gastric pain, vomiting, abdominal pain and distension, diarrhea, dysentery, borborygmus.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The saphenous nerve and the branch of the superficial peroneal nerve.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>On the medial aspect of the foot, antero- inferior to the base of the first metatarsal bone, at the border between the red and white flesh. Note: A depression can be felt when mov- ing proximally from SP3. SP4 is located in the depression distal to the base of the first metatarsal bone.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4167850</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.8 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7407065</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Gongsun</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
