    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dcterms:bibliographicCitation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 153. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 9, Acupuncture Points of the Jueyin and Shaoyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>曲澤(泽,沢)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasDesignatedSpecialPointRole"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_6594221</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Cardiac pain, palpitation, febrile diseases, irritability, stomachache, vomiting, pain in the elbow and arm, tremor of the hand and arm.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The median nerve.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>On the anterior aspect of the elbow, at the cubital crease, in the depression medial to the biceps brachii tendon. Note: When the elbow is flexed at 45 degrees, PC3 is located medial to the biceps brachii tendon.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_4694897</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture perpendicularly 0.5-0.7 inch, or prick with a three-edged needle to cause bleeding. Moxibustion is applicable.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7634323</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Quze</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
