        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 209. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 10, Acupuncture Points of the Governor and the Conception Vessels and the Extra Points. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>身柱</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Cough, asthma, epilepsy, pain and stiffness of the back, furuncles.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The medial branch of the posterior ramus of the third thoracic nerve.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>In the upper back region, in the depression inferior to the spinous process of the third thoracic vertebra (T3), on the posterior median line. Note: The depression inferior to the spinous process of the third thoracic vertebra (T3) which is at the intersection of two imaginary lines: the posterior median line and the horizontal line of the medial end of the spine of the scapula.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_0386099</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture obliquely upward 0.5-1.0 inch. Moxibustion is applicable.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_8607646</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Shenzhu</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
