        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9116386</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795319</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSurfaceLocation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9116386</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <IRI>http://uri.interlex.org/base/ilx_0795319</IRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasSynonym"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9116386</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Small Intestine 13</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasVasculatureDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9116386</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Superficially, the descending branches of the transverse cervical artery and vein; deeper, the muscular branch of the suprascapular artery and vem.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="rdfs:label"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9116386</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>SI 13</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="dcterms:bibliographicCitation"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Source for the Acupoint Location: WHO Standard Acupuncture Point Locations in the Western Pacific Region. World Health Organization. Regional Office for the Western Pacific, 2008. Page 114. ISBN 978-92-9061-248-7.

Source for Acupuncture Method, Vasculature, Innervation, and Indications:
D. Liangyue, G. Yijun, H. Shuhui, et al. Chinese Acupuncture and Moxibustion. Revised ed. Beijing: Foreign Languages Press; 1999. Chapter 8, Acupuncture Points of the Shaoyin and Taiyang Meridian. ISBN 978-7-119-01758-7.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasChineseLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>白環(环)兪(俞)</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasIndicationsDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Enuresis, pain due to hernia, morbid leukorrhea, irregular menstruation, cold sensation and pain of the lower back, dysuria, constipation, tenesmus, prolapse of the rectum.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasInnervationDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>The lateral branches of the posterior rami of the third and fourth sacral nerves, the inferior gluteal nerve.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasLocationalDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>In the sacral region, at the same level as the fourth posterior sacral foramen, 1.5 B-cun lateral to the median sacral crest. Note: 1.5 B-cun lateral to the sacral hiatus, at the same level as BL34.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMeridian"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_7525476</AbbreviatedIRI>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasMethodDescription"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Puncture perpendicularly 0.8-1.2 inches.</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
        <AnnotationProperty abbreviatedIRI="TARA:hasPinyinLabel"/>
        <AbbreviatedIRI>TARA:TARA_9128934</AbbreviatedIRI>
        <Literal>Baihuanshu</Literal>
    </AnnotationAssertion>
    <AnnotationAssertion>
